        },
        {
            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "id": "f74f8057",
            "metadata": {},
            "source": [
                "### S parameters"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "code",
            "execution_count": 4,
            "id": "80995a6c",
            "metadata": {},
            "outputs": [
                {
                    "name": "stdout",
                    "output_type": "stream",
                    "text": [
                        "loading solution from /home/weihu/moon/luminescent/runs/ring\n",
                        "may take a minute if simulation folder is remotely mounted\n"
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "data": {
                        "image/png": "",
                        "text/plain": [
                            "<Figure size 640x480 with 1 Axes>"
                        ]
                    },
                    "metadata": {},
                    "output_type": "display_data"
                }
            ],
            "source": [
                "sol = lm.load(path)\n",
                "o1=sol['monitors']['o1']\n",
                "o3=sol['monitors']['o3']\n",
                "\n",
                "S21 = o1['modes'][0]['+'] / o1['modes'][0]['-'] # drop port power, S21 aliased as S11 with mirrored source\n",
                "S31 = o3['modes'][0]['+'] / o1['modes'][0]['-'] # through port power\n",
                "\n",
                "plt.plot(wavelengths, np.abs(S21)**2, label=\"S21\")\n",
                "# plt.plot(wavelengths, S31, label=\"S31\")\n",
                "\n",
                "plt.xlabel(\"wavelength [um]\")\n",
                "plt.ylabel(\"power\")\n",
                "plt.legend()\n",
                "plt.show()"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "id": "2f6330f2",
            "metadata": {},
            "source": [
                "### Resonances"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "code",
            "execution_count": 5,
            "id": "7118a9d7",
            "metadata": {},
            "outputs": [
                {
                    "name": "stdout",
                    "output_type": "stream",
                    "text": [
                        "Peaks: 1520.00nm 1548.75nm 1577.50\n"
                    ]
                }
            ],
            "source": [
                "from scipy.signal import find_peaks\n",
                "\n",
                "dw=bandwidth/len(wavelengths)\n",
                "I, props = find_peaks(np.abs(S21), height=0.4, distance=.01//dw)\n",
                "\n",
                "peaks = wavelengths[I]\n",
                "print(f'Peaks: {\"nm \".join([ f\"{1000*x:.2f}\" for x in peaks])}')"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "id": "451226f5",
            "metadata": {},
            "source": [
                "### FSR"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "code",
            "execution_count": 6,
            "id": "06e3a231",
            "metadata": {},
            "outputs": [
                {
                    "name": "stdout",
                    "output_type": "stream",
                    "text": [
                        "FSR: 28.75nm\n"
                    ]
                }
            ],
            "source": [
                "FSR = np.mean(np.diff(peaks))\n",
                "print(f'FSR: {1000*FSR:.2f}nm')"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "id": "ff415df0",
            "metadata": {},
            "source": [
                "### Q factor (FWHM method)"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "code",
            "execution_count": 7,
            "id": "9ea20f53",
            "metadata": {},
            "outputs": [
                {
                    "name": "stdout",
                    "output_type": "stream",
                    "text": [
                        "FWHM: 5.12nm\n",
                        "Q factor (FWHM method): 302\n"
                    ]
                }
            ],
            "source": [
                "i=len(I)//2\n",
                "mid = I[i]\n",
                "half =props['peak_heights'][i]/2        # use S21[mid]-3 if S21 is in dB\n",
                "y=np.abs(S21)\n",
                "\n",
                "l = mid\n",
                "while y[l] > half: l -= 1\n",
                "wl_lo = np.interp(half, [y[l], y[l+1]], [wavelengths[l], wavelengths[l+1]])\n",
                "\n",
                "r = mid\n",
                "while y[r] > half: r += 1\n",
                "wl_hi = np.interp(half, [y[r-1], y[r]], [wavelengths[r-1], wavelengths[r]])\n",
                "\n",
                "FWHM = wl_hi - wl_lo\n",
                "wl=wavelengths[mid]\n",
                "Q=wl/FWHM\n",
                "print(f'FWHM: {1000*FWHM:.2f}nm\\nQ factor (FWHM method): {Q:.0f}')"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "id": "ba5f4b7d",
            "metadata": {},
            "source": [
                "## Early stopping (optional)\n",
                "\n",
                "Can still get FSR and Q factor by stopping early. Saves time because high Q cavity takes long time to decay completely. Instead simulate for only long enough for resonances to settle into decay trend. Here, can set `energy_decay_threshold=.1` \n",
                "\n",
                "Stopping early in time domain convolves sinc blur in frequency domain. Can still extract resonances and FSR from blurred spectrum, but Q factor must be computed from time domain decay signal."
            ]
        },
